import Layout from '../layouts/default-layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Frontend Software Engineer & Web Accessibility Specialist"
  description="Frontend software engineer and web accessibility specialist with 15+ years building for companies including Apple, Google, and PlayStation."
  image={googleCloud}
>
  <Header
    heading="Frontend Software Engineer & Web Accessibility Specialist"
    eyebrow="More than fifteen years building frontend interfaces for companies like Apple, Google, and PlayStation."
    image={googleCloud}
    imageAlt="Jade at the PlayStation office."
  >
    <p>
      I've spent more than fifteen years building frontend user interfaces,
      across freelance clients, startups, and teams at Apple, Google, and
      PlayStation. Somewhere along the way, accessibility stopped being a line
      item and became the lens I build everything through. Before I ship
      anything, I try to look at it through someone else's access need, whatever
      that calls for, like a screen reader, keyboard-only navigation, or
      captions. Design for that, and it tends to work better for everyone, not
      just the person you had in mind. This page is the fuller picture of that
      work: where I've been, what I've built, and how I think about
      accessibility and collaboration along the way.
    </p>
    <div>
      <ButtonLink href={primaryCtas.recruiterCall.href} external>
        {primaryCtas.recruiterCall.label}
      </ButtonLink>
      <ButtonLink href={resumeLink.href} external isSecondary>
        {resumeLink.label}
      </ButtonLink>
    </div>
  </Header>

  <SectionSpacer />

  <Section
    id="about"
    heading="About Me"
    eyebrow="Passion taught me the code. Perspective taught me the rest."
  >
    <p>
      Everything is connected. The way I write code is shaped by how I move
      through the world. Years of building for the web have sharpened my skills
      as an engineer, but it's my relationship with <a
        href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cKsPuNUkVzI"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">nature</a
      >, <a
        href="https://www.communalists.org/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">community</a
      >, and the <a
        href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zMqSCpWyHaw"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">spiritual</a
      > that has taught me patience, perspective, and empathy. Crafting accessible
      digital experiences is one extension of that. These values influence how I approach
      code, collaboration, and design. My aim is to create spaces that are welcoming,
      clear, and grounded in respect for others. The work is technical, but it is
      also deeply human.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <SectionSpacer />

